<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The dark counterpart the light theme never had.

    This is about the window, not about Compose. `isSystemInDarkTheme()` reads Configuration.uiMode
    and already returns the system setting whatever the platform theme is, so the Compose half works
    the moment WeboraTheme selects on it. What does not work is the window behind Compose and the
    frame drawn before the first composition: android:Theme.Material.Light is light in every
    configuration, so a user on a dark system theme got a light flash and light system-bar regions
    around dark chrome. C7 in docs/design/AUDIT.md asks for this explicitly.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Webora" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar" />
</resources>
